[Music]  [Music]  despite all the praise i've given to  breath of the wild there's one aspect to  the game which  never said well with me no it wasn't the  rain or the weapon durability system or  anything like that  in the grander scheme of things to me  personally these are about minor  nitpicks that didn't impede my enjoyment  of the overall experience  even the way the story was portrayed was  never really a big issue for me  i thought it fit well with the gameplay  making it more natural for link to just  mess around before making his way to  hyrule castle no  the real gripe i had was with calamity  ganon  i am aware that for breath of the wild  anuma and his team wanted ganon to feel  more like a force of nature  rather than an actual individual and  while i can at least  understand that decision at the same  time something felt  off about it for a being that has caused  this much destruction and suffering to  hyrule  making him so faceless and abstract  kinda takes away from the feeling of  menace felt in previous installments  zelda might not be the pinnacle of  complex storytelling and intricate  character development but we have seen  villains throughout the series who are  cunning intelligent  and downright crazy and terrifying  calamity ganon seems to lack these  elements  he's just a thing floating around he  doesn't speak and it's hard to know  exactly what he even is  besides malice turned into a physical or  spectral form  in some cases having a faceless evil  entity that we rarely see  or cannot even see its true appearance  of can be very effective  the best example i can think of would be  sauron from lord of the rings  a disembodied eye atop a massive tower  which despite its weakened state is  still able to exert a menacing dominance  over middle earth in a lot of ways  sauron and calamity ganon have a lot in  common the dark lord  sauron forged in secret a master ring  to control all others and into this ring  he poured his cruelty his malice and his  will  to dominate all life both have eyes  everywhere to perceive the world from  different vantage points  both were defeated in a battle a long  time ago and are weakened to a point  where they themselves cannot physically  manifest but rather use corruption and  manipulation to have others do their  evil bidding they infest and destroy  nature and the balance of the world  around them  but the big difference here is that  sauron is always active building armies  and using his minions to corrupt key  figures and  simply staring at him or even talking  with him can be extremely dangerous and  well his presence is just downright  terrifying  calamity ganon doesn't really impose the  same type of fear  in my opinion it's one of the reasons  why the ending to the game felt so  unfulfilling in a lot of ways  linc and zelda defeat calamity ganon and  that's it  nothing has learned no curses are cast  motivations made clear  it just ends it is perhaps the most  open-ended zelda ending  ever created and of course at the time  we didn't know that a direct sequel  which  seems to pick up right after was going  to be made which explains why it was  such an underwhelming finale  perhaps another parallel to lord of the  rings which also just ends and then  picks up in the sequel  with breath of the wild 2 now underway  things have become  a lot more clear about calamity gannon  despite barely knowing anything about  the actual story or gameplay we have at  least learned  why calamity ganon felt like such a  nothing character  it's because he was nothing just a  manifestation of hatred being controlled  from deep underground by the true source  of evil  ganondorf it's actually very reminiscent  of phantom ganon it also explains why  despite calamity ganon being such a  faceless and seemingly brainless  character  you still seem to have an actual  intelligence behind it which  is reflected by his actions and what if  calamity ganon or rather  ganondorf's plan span much further back  and even seemingly unrelated events  might be attributed to his manipulation  and strategy  this puppet master puppet dynamic  fascinates me and it's a topic that i've  been wanting to cover for a while now  so strap in as we take a look at the  potentially much bigger picture  regarding ganondorf his malice and his  plans for hyrule  the first and most obvious indication of  calamity ganon possessing a clear  intelligence is of course the corruption  of the sheikh attack itself  right before the battle of ten thousand  years ago he arose just like he did  recently  what he didn't account for however was  that the ancient shika had built a  massive army of automata to stop him in  his tracks  and as his tradition after being  weakened by this mechanized army he was  struck by the sword of evil's bane and  sealed away by princess zelda of that  era who possessed the sealing power from  goddess hylia  however as we all know now this was just  malice not the actual individual  ganondorf himself  that got sealed it is made clear  throughout the story of the game and now  by the trailer for breath wall 2  that ganondorf spends around 10 000  years to gather up enough malice to  launch  another attack or calamity if you will  upon hyrule  during these 10 000 years ganondorf had  enough time to think of a new strategy  to deal with this newfound technology  he is a very patient man a strategy he  was finally able to put into practice  100 years ago by using his malice not to  just  manifest himself but also take control  of said technology  this is a clear indication that the  brain behind calamity gannon learned  from his defeat 10 000 years ago and has  been scheming all this time  but i feel like in terms of his plans  this may be only the tip of the iceberg  and there are several hints to this some  of which have been covered by other  theorists as well  first and foremost the prophecy nintendo  black crisis already made a great video  about how the prophecy  may have been misunderstood a prophecy  that miss reg could have been a few  years after zelda was born  a still unnamed person foretold the  return of ganon  there are some suggestions that this  might have been zelda's mother the queen  of hyrule but as of right now this has  yet to be confirmed and this fortune  teller as  he or she is referred to remains totally  anonymous  here's where one thing doesn't make  sense though before the calamity was  predicted by this unknown person the  shika technology was buried and  forgotten  had this foresight never come to light  ganon would have just appeared one day  and nobody would have seen it coming  but if ganondorf's plan was to take over  the guardians and divine beast by using  his malice all along  this plan would have only worked if the  ancient chica's technology was uncovered  by the time of his return  the message the fortune teller received  was literally that the way to oppose  gallon was buried beneath the ground  which of course led to the large-scale  excavations under the command of the  royal family as far as theories go  the one that appeals to me the most is  that what if this prophecy wasn't some  divine message  but rather a manipulation by ganondorf a  message from the king of evil  himself either through some telepathic  message or as some suggest a yiga spy or  other type of  ganon loyalist posing as the fortune  teller i mean think about it the only  way for ganondorf to be able to take  control of the most powerful and  dangerous army in zelda history and  execute his plan  required this army to be unearthed he  needed this army to be found before his  rise  and by announcing his return in advance  he knew that the highlands would go out  of their way to find these ancient  relics he may have seen the sheer power  and potential of this army during the  battle of 10 000 years ago and decided  that this was the force he sought for to  eradicate the kingdom of hyrule and his  patience paid off since  well when it comes to destroying the  kingdom he came as close as you could  possibly get  where ganon failed however was in  dealing with the hero and the princess  a failure that ultimately led to his  calamity being halted once again 100  years later but this isn't to say that  he didn't try  and there are clear signs of this first  off the death of the queen of hyrule is  already pretty suspicious  her sudden and unexpected passing is a  huge red flag if you ask me  and i'm a firm believer that this wasn't  some tragic accident but rather a  conscious attempt by ganondorf to mess  with zelda's ability to awaken her  sealing power  in my video about seeing zelda  potentially becoming queen in breath of  the wild 2 i mentioned that zelda's  mother might not have possessed the  sealing power herself but rather  zelda's grandmother and her mother might  have married into the royal family and  isn't part of the original bloodline  some comments pointed out that zelda's  wording during her prayer at the spring  of wisdom  does hint that her mother did possess a  certain power too though it is not made  clear if this is indeed the sacred  ceiling power or just some other type of  ability the wording is still  vague and not very clear exactly what  zelda means and open to interpretation  in true nintendo fashion of course  however for this  theory it doesn't really matter whether  or not the queen herself possessed this  ceiling power regardless  whatever the case may be by killing off  the queen ganondorf threw a wrench in  the works and prevented zelda from  unlocking her sacred gift before the day  of the great calamity either ganondorf  killed zelda's mother because she had  mastered the ceiling power herself and  would have been able to seal him when he  rose up or wanted to deprive zelda of a  mentor who could teach her to awaken and  control set power  either way ganondorf succeeded and by  the time zelda's ability did awaken  hyrule was already devastated the death  of the queen took place when zelda was  only around 6 years old but ganondorf's  attempts at messing with the hylians  plans don't seem to stop there  this is where we get into his main focus  besides getting ready to take over  hyrule castle  namely disposing of link and zelda  ganondorf has been around since the  distant past he knows full well what the  rules are and that the keys to his  defeat lie within the presence of the  hero wielding the sword that seals the  darkness  the master sword and the one who  possesses the blood of the goddess hylia  aka princess zelda if he wanted his plan  to eradicate hyrule once and for all to  succeed he had to get rid of them  or else similar to 10 000 years ago his  attempt may fail  yet again in the months leading up to  his appearance from deep below hyrule  castle some very significant events  started taking place  for one monsters around hyrule who  previously didn't even pose a problem  anymore for the kingdom  started to grow more restless and their  numbers started to increase  and they even went as far as to attack  travelers and settlements more  frequently and seemingly more  coordinated these attacks could of  course just have been random and  monsters doing what monsters do  but at the same time this could have  also been ganon's way of trying to catch  link and zelda in the crossfire of these  attacks in hopes that one or both would  not survive to tell the tale  zelda even mentions that she believes  the intensity and frequency of these  attacks to be an omen of ganon's looming  return  little did she know her and link may  have been the main target  additionally the yiga clan also started  to become more active and even made an  attempt to kill princess zelda while she  was visiting gerudo desert and this to  me is one of the biggest indicators of  ganondorf seemingly wanting to get rid  of zelda and link before he made his  grand return  this assassination attempt was likely  him trying to get rid of princess zelda  as an extra insurance that she will not  be there to awaken her powers and seal  his malice the day he makes his move  but what about link as far as we know he  seems to be doing just fine throughout  the moments leading up to the great  calamity right  aside from him being a total badass and  slaying hordes of monsters which  attacked the kingdom he never seems to  be a direct target  with the exception of one particular  cutscene  this scene where daruk is practicing to  get divine beast varadania under his  control while being accompanied by link  has always struck me as a bit  odd after taking the beast for a spin  the two start conversing about  ganon's return the rook's motivations  link's newly appointed tasks to protect  the princess  etc when all of a sudden the ground  starts to tremble and a huge boulder is  sent hurtling down towards the two  and had it not been for the rook this  would have surely been the end of link i  mean look at this this isn't some random  landslide this single boulder is going  straight for them what are the odds that  death mountain starts shaking in this  exact location and raining down a rock  this size to the exact place where link  is standing this isn't some  huge earthquake where tons of rock are  sliding down the mountain and they just  so happen to be in the path of  destruction  one very specific pillar breaks and only  sends down a small handful of rocks  soaring down  this is just too much of a coincidence  if you ask me  even the rook comments on the  strangeness of the situation  and how death mountain has been quiet  for decades the way this is shown and  word it definitely hints that this event  has something to do with calamity  ganon's return  and the game doesn't really make a big  secret out of this but i would go a step  further and say that this wasn't just  death mountain growing more restless  because calamity ganon is returning  i would suggest that this was a direct  attempt on link's life by ganondorf to  get rid of the hero before he has a  chance to mess with his plans  and if what i proposed in my breath the  wild chronological puzzle video is true  and ganondorf has the power to create  earthquakes like he did in the past  this random event on death mountain  being a strategically planned  assassination attempt becomes more  plausible last but not least  the timing of ganon's return this one  has been covered by other creators and  theorists and while this one does have a  high probability that this was just  coincidence or unfortunate timing it is  quite peculiar how everything played out  the moment calamity ganon finally  appeared  firstly it's on the exact day that zelda  ventures to the spring of wisdom with  the five champions  basically giving him a head start as all  the pilots are now nowhere near their  divine beasts  secondly the interruption of mifa right  as she is about to tell zelda that she  thinks of the one she loves  aka link when she uses her healing power  and thus possibly revealing how zelda  could unlock her power  she is unable to finish her sentence and  mipha had she been able to say what she  wanted to say  was totally right zelda's love for link  was ultimately what caused her to  finally awaken her sacred gift but by  the time she did  most of the damage had already been done  again this could be just  unfortunate timing but you gotta admit  this was very favorable for gannon and  could just as well have been  him pulling the strings yet again all  this stuff combined the sudden rise in  monster attacks the attempts on link and  zelda's life the confusing and  suspicious prophecy  the queen's death as well as all the  other strange coincidences taking place  leads me to believe that ganondorf had a  much greater influence on the world  above ground than the game initially  reveals  the big question that remains though is  how did ganondorf  know all of this how was he able to  coordinate so well while being sealed  deep on the ground  as we learn in game and from masterworks  ganondorf uses eyes of malice to see  above ground  and even the developers made it clear  that this was purposely done to always  remind you that ganon  is everywhere and always watching so  ganondorf is basically the architect  from the matrix  however during the events of 100 years  ago no malice was yet present above  ground until after ganondorf rose from  the depths of hyrule castle how was he  able to know where zelda would be where  link would be  where to execute his monster attacks or  assassination attempts  the only way this was possible is if  someone was coordinating with ganondorf  reporting to him feeding him information  and generally being his eyes and ears  above ground  this leads me into one of my favorite  theories about breath of the wild  that the yiga may have been directly  speaking with ganondorf not calamity  ganon  but the man himself the puppet master  how exactly this is achieved is not  entirely clear one theory presented by  mass nintendo bandits suggests that the  yiga possibly dug their way down into  hyrule's underground from within their  own hideout  this hole which is found in the arena  where you fight the present-day yiga  leader master koga is very suspicious  and well  just so random why would this huge and  seemingly bottomless pit be located here  it's features definitely show that it's  something man-made  whether or not this hole was already  here or dug by the yiga themselves or  since it's also connected to a shika  shrine in the dlc maybe dug by the  ancient shika  is up for debate but it does seem like  such a weird inclusion to their hideout  this hole has to be of more importance  than we are allowed to see in game i  mean it's just too weird  another possibility is that ganondorf  has simply been able to speak with the  yiga leadership  telepathically or spiritually or  whatever you want to call it  and give them instructions on what to do  next and again this  is something he has been able to do in  the past where we can hear him speak  without him actually being in the room  the yiga are in a lot of ways a bunch of  goofballs  it's just very hard for me to imagine  that they themselves came up with the  plan to kill zelda out of nowhere their  motivations in general  are not always very clear we know that  they are at war with the gerudo and they  are loyal to ganon but ganon has at this  point not been seen for the past  10 000 years it's kinda hard to stay  loyal not to mention  motivated and pass on the information on  what to do during the next attack for  such an insanely long time  up until the prophecy the hylians and  even the current day shika had  completely forgotten about even the  existence of ganon for all intents and  purposes the yiga are but one of ganon's  pawns on the chessboard a tool he can  use to aid him while he was scheming for  his return  it's unlikely that the yiga knew all the  rules and the key elements about the  events of ten thousand years ago  to this very day the yiga might be  badass ninja assassins  from outer space no not from space but  the point is they are not competent  enough to know about all the details  about gannon what he even looks like  what his plans are  and what needs to be done unless  ganondorf has been talking to them  the yiga used to be shika so their  lifespan is about the same which is only  a bit longer than the average hylian if  not even the shika and the hylians were  able to remember the existence of ganon  how would the yiga know  anything most of the information they  got was from spying on the hylians and  the chica who also didn't know much  you get the point the sudden increase in  their activity in the months leading up  to the great calamity seems to at least  indicate that they had some  access to ganondorf's plans maybe on a  need to know basis  ganondorf's inability to dispose of  lincoln zelda during and before the  great calamity  ultimately led to the defeat of his  malice puppet 100 years later however  this isn't to say that this was the  extent of his plans  perhaps breath the while 2 will reveal  ganondorf's plan b  and for all we know lincoln zelda's  little cave adventure which leads them  to finding his corpse is  all part of the plan maybe it's  ganondorf who sets them on this path and  wants to be found so he can break free  from his seal whatever the case may be  i am very excited to see what happens  and i'm also hoping that the game will  shed some more light on the events  during the backstory of brethwald who  this mysterious fortune teller was  why the queen died so suddenly and  unexpectedly since this is a direct  sequel we could see some of these events  play out from the perspective of  ganondorf  and if he is properly voiced which i  really hope he will be  he could explain more about himself and  his motivations like he did in twilight  princess and the wind waker  and that is all for now let me know in  the comments what you think of this  whole situation  what will ganondorf's plans be in breath  of the wild too will we see his malice  play another major role or will nintendo  tone this down  and focus on something else something  new perhaps  as always a big thanks to my patreons of  which i have a couple of new ones  joining the maze so  please welcome austin barrett jasper  freyka  legend of levy charles zazz as well as  an honorable mention to  steven and parker who just upgraded his  pledge thank you all  very much you beautiful people you i  will see you all next week for some more  zelda goodness and also look forward to  my paper mario the origami king review  very soon i hope you all have a  wonderful weekend and  this is don signing off have a good one

